[thin] Accepted wing-retention lips: each row is the flat lip over a sideways wing slot of the DATA plate or nameplate receiver, 1.23 mm thick (plate 3.36 - wing 1.68 - 0.45 air), thinning to 0.83 mm at the slot mouth along the 1.10 x 0.40 mm entry bevel; the lint reads it 1.01 mm through, partway up the bevel. `plain_lips` keeps the flutes off it. This receiver geometry is the one physically accepted on 2026-09-30 (nameplate/horizontal-wing-trial/physical-acceptance.json).
alternatives: A thicker lip needs a thicker plate or a thinner wing, each a change to the accepted fit.
