click: x=97.375 y=338.300 z=259.400
click: x=97.375 y=338.800 z=327.200

[ledge] Unavoidable fitted catch bridges: each face is the bearing face of a catch window in `carb-1`'s or `co2-2`'s capped rib under the ceiling, where the anchor cap's lip bears. Back-top prints ceiling-down, so the rib stands up off the slab and the face prints as a 10.3 mm bridge between the rib's two 3 mm end webs (`_anchor_cap_interface`: the cap's 10 mm and a slip at each end), roofing the closed pocket the lip enters.
alternatives: A corbel or column under the face fills the window the lip enters. Sloping the face turns the lip's pull into a spread that walks the wing out of the window, and a window open at its ends gives up the end webs the bridge stands on.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
